<!--
  ClickHouse ships a dozen system.*_log tables on by default. On a laptop they
  are the single largest consumer of both disk and background merge work on a
  server that is otherwise nearly idle: metric_log alone writes a row per second
  per metric.

  Two things about this file are load-bearing:

  1. It MUST be in config.d, not config.xml. Editing the main config does not
     remove these tables; they get created anyway. (ClickHouse#62716.)
  2. The "z" prefix. config.d loads alphabetically, and a remove="1" only takes
     effect if it is applied after the definition it removes.

  query_log is deliberately KEPT, bounded by a 1 day TTL rather than deleted.
  This is an observability platform; a hot store that discards the record of its
  own queries would be a bad joke, and it is what makes "why was that dashboard
  panel slow" answerable at all. It is also the cheapest of the set, since rows
  are written per query rather than per second.

  (XML comments cannot contain a double hyphen, so no em dashes in this file.)
-->
<clickhouse>
    <query_log>
        <ttl>event_date + INTERVAL 1 DAY DELETE</ttl>
        <flush_interval_milliseconds>30000</flush_interval_milliseconds>
    </query_log>

    <metric_log remove="1"/>
    <asynchronous_metric_log remove="1"/>
    <trace_log remove="1"/>
    <part_log remove="1"/>
    <text_log remove="1"/>
    <session_log remove="1"/>
    <query_thread_log remove="1"/>
    <query_views_log remove="1"/>
    <processors_profile_log remove="1"/>
    <error_log remove="1"/>
    <latency_log remove="1"/>
</clickhouse>
